# Stay Safe Online -- Checklist (College Students, India)

## Personal Security

-   Use strong, unique passwords for each account; consider a password
    manager.
-   Enable 2-factor authentication (2FA) on email, social media, and
    banking apps.
-   Do not share OTPs, passwords, or PINs with anyone---even if they
    claim to be from a bank.
-   Keep your devices updated with the latest security patches and
    antivirus software.
-   Avoid using public Wi-Fi for sensitive activities; use a VPN if
    necessary.

## Social Media Awareness

-   Review privacy settings regularly and limit personal information
    visibility.
-   Do not accept friend requests from unknown people.
-   Be cautious of phishing links sent via messages or emails.

## Financial / UPI Safety

-   Verify UPI payment requests carefully before approving; never accept
    unknown "collect" requests.
-   Double-check QR codes before scanning---fraudsters may replace them
    with fake ones.
-   Do not install unknown screen-sharing apps when asked by "customer
    care".
-   Use official banking/UPI apps only (like BHIM, Google Pay, PhonePe).

## Device & App Safety

-   Download apps only from official app stores (Google Play Store,
    Apple App Store).
-   Check app permissions and avoid granting unnecessary access.
-   Log out from shared/public computers after use.

## Reporting Cybercrime

-   Report incidents immediately at the National Cyber Crime Portal:
    https://cybercrime.gov.in
-   Call the Cyber Crime Helpline: 1930 for urgent financial fraud
    reporting.

## Quick Habits

-   Regularly monitor bank statements and transaction alerts.
-   Backup important data securely (cloud or external drive).
-   Stay informed about latest cyber fraud techniques.

Stay alert. Think before you click.
